# I03.var03 FTMO reviewer correction — 2026-10-08

I initially called the prospective design's `FTMO=2` integral wrong because I summed four half-hour report row values `1+1+1+1=4` without multiplying by each interval's width. That objection was an error in my review, not a source or report defect. I sent the incorrect message to root and author, then retracted it before the prospective contract was frozen. The unchanged design v2 is `tmp/i03-var03-batch-contract-design-v2-20261008.md` (11,762 bytes, SHA-256 `d0cbfd3569a037580f9589e069a3823b01aa2e4c93157812a984539f35ddbf61`).

The accepted I03.var01 control and OUT SystemResults each have `FTMO=1` in four half-hour operation bins. The raw row-value sum is 4; the **time integral** is `4 × 0.5 h = 2 h`. The installed SIMLOX manual PDF pp.642–643 calls FTMO the fraction of calendar time in mission operation for each system, a state-type average, and excludes premission assignment and turnround. Frozen I03.var02 `report_oracle.py` computes `FTMO=mission/2` for this exact two-aircraft unit. This bounded per-system fraction is distinct from `NSYMO=2` in those bins and its aircraft-count integral `4 aircraft-hours`.

Therefore the matched control and child both prospectively have integrated `FTMO=2` under the two-wave, two-aircraft, one-hour-per-wave hypothesis. Full source/event interval reconciliation remains required; neither the accepted rows nor this correction accept a future native report. The design still needs an exact h7.75 boundary rule and explicit classification of all remaining report fields before contract freeze.
